// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root-cause of 0% accuracy in attempts 69-70: the math expression grammar
// accepts bare identifiers (e.g. `["n1"]`) as IsCompletePrefix, so the eager
// close fires after just 1 token, producing 15+ tiny `<<n1>>` spans per
// example. The evaluator extracts the LAST visible span; that is always a
// sub-expression, never the complete answer.
//
// Two-part fix:
//   1. EOS-penalty gate: while |currentConstrainedOut| < minSpanLen, use
//      PenalizedConstrainedStep with eosToken penalised by -8.0. The hard mask
//      still allows EOS only when the parser says it is valid, but the heavy
//      penalty makes the model strongly prefer extending the expression with an
//      operator and more terms, preventing premature bare-variable closure.
//   2. Minimum-length guard: CloseConstrainedSpan (eager close) is attempted
//      only when |currentConstrainedOut| >= minSpanLen.  Above that threshold
//      AdaptiveConstrainedStep runs normally and EOS + CloseSpanWithinBudget
//      handles termination cleanly.
//
// All <<detection uses RenderedEndsWith (required). Budget-pressure paths and
// force-open-at-end are kept from the 40.8% best attempt. Guidance instructs
// the model to combine all terms into one span.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Outside + UnconstrainedStep / RenderedEndsWith branch:
//     EnterObservedConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := []; parser.IsValidPrefix([])
//     holds by method precondition. ✓
//   Outside + OpenConstrainedSpan (budget pressure):
//     Same: currentConstrainedOut := [], IsValidPrefix([]) holds. ✓
//   CloseConstrainedSpan branch (complete, len >= minSpanLen):
//     Sets insideConstrainedOut := false, making the implication vacuous;
//     currentConstrainedOut cleared to []. ✓
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget branches (budget-pressure close, or EOS-triggered close):
//     Postcondition directly guarantees
//     insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut). ✓
//   PenalizedConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken (span short):
//     PenalizedConstrainedStep hard-masks to parser-valid tokens plus EOS;
//     non-EOS return satisfies IsTokenValidNext; AppendConstrainedToken extends
//     currentConstrainedOut by that token, preserving IsValidPrefix. ✓
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken (span long):
//     Same argument — hard mask guarantees the token is parser-valid. ✓
//
// Invariant 2 — progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Init: equality at steps == 0. ✓
//   UnconstrainedStep + append: steps += 1, |generated| += 1. ✓
//   UnconstrainedStep + EOS break: steps += 1, |generated| unchanged. ✓
//   OpenConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, |generated| += 1 (the `<<` token). ✓
//   CloseConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, |generated| grows by at most 1 (`>>`). ✓
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget (closeBudget = maxSteps - steps): helper postcondition
//     gives |generatedOut| <= |generated| + closeBudget; after steps := maxSteps,
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + old_steps + (maxSteps - old_steps)
//     = |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps = |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//   PenalizedConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken: steps += 1, |generated|
//     += 1. ✓
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken: steps += 1, |generated|
//     += 1. ✓
//   EOS path + CloseSpanWithinBudget: one step consumed by the constrained-step
//     helper, then steps := maxSteps; |generated| grows by at most
//     (maxSteps - steps_after_helper) which equals old closeBudget - 1, so
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

